body:
I'd like to replace the `facetName`  prop by a `facet` prop, with a `name` attribute but possibly other ones.

The issue this would solve here would be to be able to have a label associated to the facet name and be able to display it in the header.

Currently, here is what we're using:

``` js
for facet in facets:
  myWidget({
    facetName: facet.name,
    templates: {
      header:  '<div class="my-header">' + facet.title + '</div>'
  });
```

I'd like us to be able to have:

``` js
var headerTemplate = '<div class="my-header">{{ facet.title }}</div>';

for facet in facets:
  myWidget({
    facet: facet,
    templates: {
      header:  headerTemplate
  });
```

which would feel more in adequation with what `headerFooter` has been designed for.

comments.body:
Not sure we want to change the `facetName` behavior, it's more complex to use with an object because you can pass whatever you want.

I think what you want is the ability to add more data to the underlying templates, so maybe we could just do something like:

``` js
for facet in facets:
  myWidget({
    facetName: facet.name,
    templatesData: facet,
    templates: {
      header: headerTemplate
  });
```

or 

``` js
for facet in facets:
  myWidget({
    facetName: facet.name,
    templates: {
      header: prepare(headerTemplate, facet) //  replace(/FACET_TITLE/g, facet.title) or something
  });
```

What do you think?
